==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Hip Hop Cat's slow chance from 10% to 40%.
*Can Can Cat was among the units that were given [[Immune to Warp]] in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Hip Hop Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Hip Hop Cat
Flunking student from a certain dance school.
Can be produced in masses. Flash Mob!
Might slow Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Dancing Flasher Cat
Someone you don't want to see on the street.
Dances skillfully to keep the game kid-friendly.
Might slow Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Can Can Cat
Kicked out of dance school for improvising
performances too provocative for family shows.
Sometimes slows movement of Red enemies.</pre>
*Hip Hop Cat's Japanese name, Catxile, is a reference to the Japanese boy band [[wikipedia:Exile (Japanese band)|EXILE]]; its walking animation is one of the dance moves associated with their song "[https://youtu.be/0rDGmAqv81U Rising Sun]" (0:31); and its idle animation is taken from the beginning of "[https://youtu.be/BDGUaK0SpqA Choo Choo Train]" (0:08).
**Hip Hop Cat's English name is inaccurate in this regard, as EXILE isn't a hip-hop group.
*Can Can Cat gets its name from [[wikipedia:Can-can|can-can]], a high energy dance which typically sees dancers dressed in a similar outfit to Can Can Cat's.
*The kanji on Dancing Flasher Cat's fans is 祭, meaning festival.
**In the Taiwanese and Korean versions, the kanji on the fans are replaced with stars.
*Hip Hop Cat's base health stat is the same as its base attack stat. This is true for each of its forms.
*[[Suntan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Suntan Cat]]'s Japanese description states that he joined the Great Cat War because of his admiration for Hip Hop Cat.
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Dancing Flasher Cat and [[Evil Cat (Rare Cat)|Gentleman Cat]] both have their names shortened to Flasher Cat.

